Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(geometry): real road paths via ORS, cached on edges
 (day-14, 0003)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Roads stop being straight lines: geometry is computed once per EDGE by
OpenRouteService (driving-hgv), cached in a new network_edges.geometry_json
column, and inherited by every leg the dripper materializes over that
edge — the day-12d pattern generalized to land modes.

- migration c5e6f7a8b9d0 (batch_alter_table; downgrade drops)
- services/land_geometry.py: parse_ors_geojson (pure, shape-strict) +
  ors_road_route (never raises, 12 s timeout, warns on HTTP != 200) +
  fill_road_edge_geometries (only NULL-geometry edges, 0.25 s politeness
  sleep for the 2,000 req/day free tier; no key -> no_key stat, exit-2
  semantics via scripts/25 — mirrors script 17)
- scripts/25_build_land_geometry.py: thin CLI (re-run is cheap: filled
  edges are skipped)
- dripper: _load_caches preloads the edge-geometry map; _leg_geometry
  returns cached edge geometry verbatim BEFORE any fallback; missing
  edge geometry keeps the documented day-12d behaviour (AIR arc, else
  straight)
- RAIL intentionally not filled: Overpass corridors for ~750 km hauls
  need the OSM rail-graph builder (follow-up); column + precedence are
  mode-agnostic so rail lands without further code changes
- tests: ORS parse (happy + 3 bad shapes), edge-geometry precedence
  (verbatim reuse, both modes), unchanged fallbacks (arc/straight)

Gates: 544 unit / 184 integration; migration on both DBs; live drip
smoke OK (no-key path degrades to straight, no crash).
